---
import CourseLayout from "../layouts/CourseLayout.astro";
import ReserveDiagram from "../components/ReserveDiagram.astro";
import AssessmentSummary from "../components/AssessmentSummary.astro";
import Activity from "../components/Activity.astro";
import {outcomes} from "../data/academy";
import {withBase} from "astro-theme-university/url";
import {courseMeta} from "../course-config";
---
<CourseLayout title={courseMeta.title} description={courseMeta.description} home>
<section class="hero-board">
 <div><p class="eyebrow">SLOP UNIVERSITY / IMPOSSIBLE OPERATIONS</p><h1>MASTERMIND<span>The Art of the Impossible Heist</span></h1><p class="intro">The first plan gets you into the room.<br/>The second proves you belong there.</p><p>Fictional heist planning for fourth-year systems thinkers.<br/>Twelve weeks. One operation at the Grand Reserve.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href={withBase("/lectures/")}>Explore the course ↗</a><a class="button ghost" href={withBase("/operation/")}>Enter the Operation Room</a></div></div>
 <div class="hero-art"><ReserveDiagram /></div>
</section>
<div class="hero-footer"><span>OPERATION 408 / GLASS CROWN</span><span>TARGET: THE GRAND RESERVE</span><span>12 WEEKS · 2027</span></div>
<div class="section-grid"><section><span class="section-number">01 / THE COMMISSION</span><h2>The prize is simple.<br/>Everything else changes.</h2><p>The Grand Reserve holds a Crown that authenticates an entire city’s ownership records. Your crew has been asked to extract it. First, you must establish what that would actually mean.</p><p>Build an evidence ledger. Model an invented seal system. Negotiate a crew agreement. Then face the document that makes your carefully assembled plan obsolete.</p><p>This is an original fictional academy for students who enjoy intricate puzzles, ensemble stories and decisions that resist an easy answer.</p></section><section><span class="section-number">02 / THE DOCTRINE</span><blockquote>A successful outcome can conceal a bad decision. A failed operation can expose a good one.</blockquote><p>You are assessed on evidence, reasoning and revision. The rehearsal’s ending never determines your academic grade.</p><p class="small">Fourth-year undergraduate level. Basic logical reasoning and a willingness to explain your choices are enough. No programming or security background is required.</p></section></div>
<section><p class="eyebrow">THE SEMESTER IN THREE ACTS</p><h2>Build it. Break it. Defend it.</h2><div class="section-grid"><div><h3>01—06 / The first plan</h3><p>Define the job, inspect the evidence, learn the symbolic systems and assemble the crew. Preserve Version 1.</p><h3>07 / Break the Mastermind</h3><p>A signed revision changes one dependency. Trace its effects and build Version 2 without erasing your earlier reasoning.</p></div><div><h3>08—12 / Beyond the Architect</h3><p>Reconcile an incomplete record. Hear a refusal. Reconsider the prize. Test against a rival, then defend the final operation.</p><a class="button" href={withBase("/lectures/")}>Read the twelve-week schedule</a></div></div></section>
<section><p class="eyebrow">WHAT YOU WILL LEARN</p><h2>Six capabilities. One operation.</h2><ol class="outcome-list">{outcomes.map(([id,title,body])=><li><span>{id}</span><div><strong>{title}</strong><span>{body}</span></div></li>)}</ol></section>
<div class="section-grid"><section><h2>A real course rhythm.</h2><p>Monday: a one-hour briefing. Friday: a two-hour lab. Allow around three more hours for preparation and assessment work.</p><p>Teaching runs from 22 February to 28 May 2027, with a pause from 5–18 April. Every week produces something your later work needs.</p><p>All materials are open. Start anywhere; samples are available when you need earlier context.</p></section><section><h2>Assessment</h2><AssessmentSummary /></section></div>
<section><p class="eyebrow">TRY A PIECE OF THE TRAINING</p><h2>Would you trust this evidence?</h2><p>Three statements. Three different relationships to the truth. This is the Week 2 exercise; anything you save joins your local dossier.</p><Activity week={2}/><p><a href={withBase("/operation/")}>Open or export your dossier</a></p></section>
<section><h2>Your instructors</h2><p>Mara Voss builds the plan. Iona Vale finds the unsupported assumption. Sol Renn makes sure the record survives both of them.</p><a href={withBase("/people/")}>Meet the fictional teaching team ↗</a></section>
</CourseLayout>
